  "equipment_type": "Energy meter",
  "applies_to": "Eastron SDM230-DI single-phase 100 A DIN-rail meter with two digital inputs and RS485 Modbus RTU, manual 2025 V1.00.",
  "summary": "The SDM230-DI is a single-phase, direct-connected (up to 100 A) DIN-rail energy meter with two digital inputs and an RS485 Modbus RTU port. Measurements, demand and energy totals are 32-bit IEEE floats in input registers (function 04); settings are held in holding registers (function 03 read, 16 write). This map covers the electrical values, import/export and resettable energy, demand, RS485 settings and the measurement-mode selector.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "Registers are printed Modicon style (30001, 40003, six-digit 463777...) next to the hex start address sent on the wire. Wire address = printed number minus 30001 / 40001 / 400001; the manual's example reads 40003 at start address 0x0002."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "SDM230-DI User Manual",
    "doc_number": "2025 V1.00",
    "revision_date": "2025-06-04",
    "url": "https://www.eastrongroup.com/eastrongroup/2025/06/17/eastronsdm230-diusermanualv1.00.pdf",
    "pages": "Chapter 5, pp. 16-23 (PDF pages 19-26)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Word order: the manual states that floats are sent big-endian with the first register holding the high 16 bits, and its example returns 42 70 00 00 for 60 minutes. All floats here are ABCD.",
    "The input table footnote says total kWh/kVArh is import plus export; the measurement-mode register (463777) can change how the meter forms its total, so check that setting if totals look wrong.",
    "Left out: Int64 energy (Wh / VArh, from 310001) and Int32 scaled readings (from 310251), because the manual states big-endian order only for floats.",
    "Left out: DI-1/DI-2 counters (40770/40772) and serial number (464513), unsigned 32-bit values with no stated word order.",
    "The reset register also lists a kWh reset code, but the code is blank in the manual, so only the demand (0000) and DI-count (0006) codes are given.",
    "Demand footnote: the manual says the power-sum demand is calculated for 'import – export' (en dash) without saying whether that means net import minus export or both directions combined; check on a live meter if the sign matters."
  ],
